# What each composer removed from a composed layer, per quantity. One row per
# (composition, composed layer, quantity): the amount taken out because two parts counted it
# twice, the typed reason it could not be sized, or the identity that computes it.
#
# The only entry that makes a number smaller
#   An elimination is the only entry in this model that makes a number smaller, and this is the
#   wrapper the rest of this directory is built on. `composition/fused.sqlc` and
#   `queries/matrices/3b-composed-quantities.sqlc` both need the same three-clause join into
#   `pm.elimination` (composition, composed layer, quantity); written out in each
#   file, it is the same join character for character, differing only in which alias it binds to.
#
# The zero-fill is deliberately absent
#   `coalesce(low, 0)` reads "nothing was eliminated", which is true only after
#   `composition/owed_equality.sqlc` has already removed the fusions that owe no sum. A composer who
#   says "these hours are double counted and cannot say by how much" files `absent = 'unmeasured'`,
#   and coalescing that to zero asserts a reconciliation they explicitly declined to make. The
#   absence is carried; the caller decides.
#
# `quantity` is a column
#   An elimination is per quantity. Demand may be double counted while the nameplate is not: two
#   teams sharing one machine overlap in what they ask of it and not in what it can make. Filtering
#   to `'demand'` is a caller's question, not this relation's.
#
# `claim_seq` is how an elimination reaches its own edge
#   A claim's `narrowsWhen` and `boundOrigin` are keyed on the claim's position in the document, and
#   this table is keyed on a fusion and a quantity, so the ordinal is the only join between an
#   eliminated figure and what its filer said about who set its bound. It is NULL exactly where the
#   quantity is not a claim. Carried here rather than looked up by a reader, because the figures
#   cannot recover it: two eliminations of one filing may hold the same three points in the same
#   unit.
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:eliminations/asrt:elimination, per composed layer and quantity.
SELECT e.composition, e.composed_layer, e.quantity,
       e.low, e.mode, e.high, e.unit,
       e.absent, e.derivation, e.reason, e.claim_seq
FROM pm.elimination e
